; Part of ferrum. MIT licence, see ferrum/LICENSE.
; Broken tool check on the tool setter (TOOLS › CHECK, and a job's TOOL
; CHECK op): o<ferrum_tool_check> call. No arguments. Measures the tool
; in the spindle on the setter, the same way as o<tool_touch_off>, and
; compares the result with its tool table length. It does not change the
; table. Prints
;   (DEBUG, FERRUM-TOOLCHECK T=<tool> LENGTH=<measured> TABLE=<table> TOL=<#3037>)
;  and aborts when the two differ by more than the breakage tolerance
; #3037 (the abort text has the numbers: an abort drops the queued DEBUG): shorter means the tool broke or chipped, longer that it slipped
; in the holder or the wrong tool is in. A program running it stops there.
; Checks first: a tool is loaded and it is not the probe #3014, #3010 > 0,
; #3037 > 0, and the setter settings (o<ferrum_setter_ready>). Motion as
; o<tool_touch_off>: spindle stop, G49, machine Z 0, G30 X/Y, touch,
; back to machine Z 0. Afterwards the modal state is as it was (M73).
; Works in machine units.
o<ferrum_tool_check> sub
o10 if [#<_task> EQ 0]
    o<ferrum_tool_check> return
o10 endif
o100 if [#5400 LE 0]
    (ABORT, No tool in the spindle to check)
o100 endif
o110 if [#5400 EQ #3014]
    (ABORT, The probe is in the spindle: the setter checks cutting tools only)
o110 endif
o120 if [#3010 LE 0]
    (ABORT, Measure the spindle nose reference height first)
o120 endif
o130 if [#3037 LE 0]
    (ABORT, Set the tool setter breakage tolerance first: it must be positive)
o130 endif
o<ferrum_setter_ready> call

#<tool> = #5400
M5
M73
M50 P0
; The table length of the loaded tool: what G43 would apply.
G43 H#<tool>
#<table> = #5403
o140 if [#<table> LE 0]
    (ABORT, This tool has no length in the tool table yet: measure it first)
o140 endif
o<ferrum_setter_touch> call [#5410 / 2]
#<length> = [#<_value> + #3010]
(DEBUG, FERRUM-TOOLCHECK T=#<tool> LENGTH=#<length> TABLE=#<table> TOL=#3037)
; Wait for the retract to machine Z 0 to finish (M66 waits for motion):
; an abort would drop it with the DEBUG line and leave the tool down at the
; setter. The abort says the numbers itself for the same reason.
M66 E0 L0
o200 if [#<length> LT [#<table> - #3037]]
    (ABORT, Tool check: T%d#<tool> may be broken. It measured %.4f#<length>, the table says #<table>)
o200 endif
o210 if [#<length> GT [#<table> + #3037]]
    (ABORT, Tool check: T%d#<tool> is longer than its table length, it may have slipped in the holder. It measured %.4f#<length>, the table says #<table>)
o210 endif
o<ferrum_tool_check> endsub
M2
